======================================================================
K1. Idempotency key: SET idem:<txn_ref> NX EX 86400
======================================================================
  attempt 1: SET NX -> True  ->  process the cash-out
  attempt 2: SET NX -> None  ->  duplicate retry, return stored result, do NOT debit again
  attempt 3: SET NX -> None  ->  duplicate retry, return stored result, do NOT debit again
  TTL idem:R261104000000777 = 86400 seconds

======================================================================
K2. Atomic check-and-increment of an agent's daily cash-out total (Lua)
======================================================================
  20 concurrent cash-outs of N10,000 against a N100,000 limit
  approved: 10  rejected: 10  final total: N100,000
  key expires at midnight: TTL 31842 s
  (Redis runs each Lua script atomically on its single command thread, so there is no write skew
   without locks. Compare Portfolio 3 D10, where PostgreSQL needed SERIALIZABLE or a row lock.)

